      "Language": "dut",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A 81-year-old woman presented at the emergency department with a painful right arm due to a comminuted fracture of the humeral head. Operation was postponed because of a wound and vulnerable skin due to a large hematoma. By the time of the operation, the humeral head had migrated subcutaneously which resulted in a solid swelling of the upper arm."},
